// AN INVISIBLE TYPE IS NOT NAMED OUTSIDE ITS FILE (`@FR-F-Visible`).  A type that is not `pub` and
// that no `pub` item of its file names is INVISIBLE outside it: it cannot even be named, so a
// signature that names it reads as naming a type that is not there — and says nothing of the
// library's private declarations.  The fixture library's `VeSeed` is used only by a private
// function.  This refusal comes a compile pass before the others of this rule, so it has its own
// file; they are `what-has-no-pub-consent-is-refused-outside-its-file-refused.loft`.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard: refused as the rule says on the tree of the suite pin
//   that adds this cell, interpret and native-c; a corrupted expectation fails the file.
//   CHANNEL: the expected error (it must be met, and nothing else may be reported).
//   ARMED: every run.
//   HOLDS: the Rust twin `an_invisible_type_is_not_named` in tests/pub_visibility.rs.
//
// @EXPECT_ERROR: Undefined type VeSeed

use f_visible_fixture_lib::*;

fn take_a_seed(s: VeSeed) -> integer { 1 }
